NoovexOS Bluetooth (drivers/bluetooth)

btusb.c, hci.c, hci_parse.h
  Own code (NoovexOS project, GPLv3 like the rest of the OS). Written from the
  Bluetooth Core Specification (Vol 4 Part B, USB transport; Vol 4 Part E, HCI).

rtlbt_fw.c, rtlbt_fw.h
  Port of FreeBSD usr.sbin/bluetooth/rtlbtfw (rtlbt_fw.c, rtlbt_hw.c, main.c).
  SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
  Copyright (c) 2013 Adrian Chadd <adrian@freebsd.org>
  Copyright (c) 2019 Vladimir Kondratyev <wulf@FreeBSD.org>
  Copyright (c) 2023 Future Crew LLC.
  The full BSD-2-Clause text is kept at the top of both files.
  Cross-checked against Linux drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c (GPL-2.0-or-later,
  used as a reference only). One deliberate difference from FreeBSD: a V2
  security subsection whose key id matches the chip is included in the patch
  (as Linux btrtl does); FreeBSD stops at it. The config file is appended
  whenever present (as FreeBSD and Linux do).
  The chip table (15 entries with the CONFIG / MSFT flags) and the list of 58
  non-Realtek-vendor USB ids are taken from FreeBSD rtlbt_fw.c / main.c
  (BSD-2-Clause, fetched from freebsd-src main). Differences: RTLBT_IC_FLAG_SIMPLE
  is a real bit here (FreeBSD defines it as 0, so its 8723A path never runs):
  an 8723A file is sent raw, without ROM query or config, and an epatch file is
  refused for it (as Linux btrtl does). 8821C and 8822C keep the built-in
  firmware; every other chip loads /lib/firmware/rtl_bt/<name>.

Firmware: assets/firmware/rtl_bt/
  rtl8821c_fw.bin, rtl8821c_config.bin, rtl8822cu_fw.bin, rtl8761bu_config.bin
  (rtl8761bu_config.bin is what linux-firmware links rtl_bt/rtl8822cu_config.bin to).
  From linux-firmware (git.kernel.org/.../firmware/linux-firmware.git, WHENCE
  entry "Driver: btusb - Bluetooth USB driver").
  Licence: Redistributable. See LICENCE.rtlwifi_firmware.txt (next to the files).
  SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-LICENCE.rtlwifi_firmware.txt
  The blobs are shipped unmodified.

intelbt_fw.c, intelbt_fw.h
  Port of FreeBSD usr.sbin/bluetooth/iwmbtfw (iwmbt_fw.c, iwmbt_hw.c, main.c).
  SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
  Copyright (c) 2013 Adrian Chadd <adrian@freebsd.org>
  Copyright (c) 2019 Vladimir Kondratyev <wulf@FreeBSD.org>
  Copyright (c) 2023 Future Crew LLC.
  The full BSD-2-Clause text is kept at the top of both files.
  Deliberate differences from FreeBSD: TLV entries with a wrong length are
  rejected instead of assert(); hardware variants 0x15/0x16 are refused (FreeBSD
  leaves the header length unset); a DDC record is sent whole (length byte plus
  data, as Linux btintel does); the boot event after Intel Reset is awaited for
  up to 5 s; secure-send acks are accepted from the bulk or the interrupt pipe.
  Firmware: not shipped. Loaded at run time from /lib/firmware/intel/
  (ibt-*.sfi, ibt-*.ddc, ibt-hw-*.bseq) from linux-firmware if the user has it.
mtkbt_fw.c, mtkbt_fw.h
  MediaTek MT79xx (MT7921/MT7922/MT7925/MT7902/MT6639) USB Bluetooth firmware
  download, ported from Linux drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.c and btmtk.h
  (patch header and section map layout, WMT vendor command 0xFC6F, WMT event
  poll on the control pipe, section download, endpoint reset option, function
  on, firmware file naming).
  SPDX-License-Identifier: ISC
  Copyright (C) 2021 MediaTek Inc.
  The full ISC text is kept at the top of both files.
  The USB id list was taken as facts from Linux drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c.
  Firmware is not shipped: it is read from /lib/firmware/mediatek/... if present
  (linux-firmware, LICENCE.mediatek).
bcmbt_fw.c, bcmbt_fw.h
  Broadcom BCM20702/BCM43xx USB patchram loader, derived from Linux
  drivers/bluetooth/btbcm.c (SPDX line verified on the fetched file).
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
  Copyright (C) 2015  Intel Corporation
  The Broadcom USB ID/vendor list (vendor-specific 0xFF/0x01/0x01 interfaces)
  follows the facts in Linux drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c (GPL-2.0-or-later).
  Firmware: NOT shipped. Broadcom .hcd patch files are not in linux-firmware
  and are not redistributable; they are read at run time from
  /lib/firmware/brcm/<chip>-<vid>-<pid>.hcd, BCM-<vid>-<pid>.hcd or <chip>.hcd
  when present. Without them the controller keeps running its ROM firmware.
